-- P27b The Code That Lies - Stage 4
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Debug Console - Execution Trace","dataPayload":"EXECUTION TRACE, vault delta door frame console, four steps indexed from zero: STEP 0, REGISTER ZERO, INPUT ONE, WRITES STATE ONE - marked GOOD. STEP 1, REGISTER ONE, INPUT ONE, WRITES STATE TWO - marked SUSPECT. STEP 2, REGISTER TWO, INPUT THREE, WRITES STATE THREE - marked GOOD. STEP 3, REGISTER THREE, INPUT TWO, WRITES STATE TWO - marked GOOD. Every input and every written state on this trace is printed in decimal; the console prints no other notation.","visualType":"console","whatTheySee":"A four-step trace with one step marked suspect, all values written as plain decimal digits.","taskPrompt":"Record all four steps with their register, input and written state exactly as printed.","intermediateOutput":"Four steps, one suspect; all values decimal."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Trace Anomaly Detector - The Contradiction","dataPayload":"ANOMALY DETECTOR: the console prints its own assertion beside the trace - THE TRACE IS FAITHFUL TO THE RECORD. Compare the assertion against the steps. A faithful machine writes the input it was given into the register; step 0 wrote one from one, step 2 wrote three from three, step 3 wrote two from two. Step 1 was given one and wrote two: the register advanced by one instead of holding its input. The trace contradicts its own assertion, and the contradiction is the evidence - the trace is not faithful, it is an assertion wearing a trace''s clothes. Re-simulate with step 1 corrected to hold its input: the register sequence becomes one, one, three, two from a clean start. The write that must be patched is the one at step 1, and the patch console addresses registers in hexadecimal, two digits, upper case.","visualType":"timeline","whatTheySee":"An anomaly detector pitting the console''s own faithfulness assertion against the four printed steps.","taskPrompt":"Find the step that contradicts the assertion and report the register it wrote, in decimal.","intermediateOutput":"Step 1 contradicts the assertion; corrected re-simulation gives one, one, three, two; the register to patch is step 1''s."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Memory Patch Terminal - Address Field","dataPayload":"MEMORY PATCH TERMINAL: ADDRESS: [ _ _ ]. The terminal takes a register address in two-digit hexadecimal, upper case, and nothing else. The trace and the re-simulation are reproduced above it, all in decimal.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A two-digit hexadecimal address field on the patch terminal, above a decimal trace.","taskPrompt":"Convert the register address of the step to be patched into two-digit hexadecimal and submit it.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The memory patch terminal with its two-digit hexadecimal field, the four-step decimal trace, and the anomaly detector''s re-simulation.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the decimal trace; the Analyst finds the step that contradicts the console''s own assertion and fixes the register to patch; the Operator converts that register address into the terminal''s hexadecimal format and submits it.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records all four steps with registers, inputs and written states in decimal.","analystDiscovery":"Identifies step 1 as the contradiction and derives that its register is the one to patch."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the four decimal trace steps and the suspect flag on step 1.","analystTransforms":"Analyst tests the trace against the console''s faithfulness assertion and isolates the register to patch.","operatorExecutes":"Operator converts the register address to two-digit hexadecimal and submits it, unlocking P28."},"hints":["Do not trust the SUSPECT flag on its own - the console also prints an assertion that the trace is faithful to the record. Test every step against that assertion.","A faithful machine writes the input it was given. One step was given one value and wrote another; that step, not the flag, is the corruption.","You have the register number in decimal. The patch terminal will not accept decimal - it wants the same address as two upper-case hexadecimal digits, and the register you patch is the corrupted step''s own."],"narrativeObjective":"Catch the trace in its own lie and patch the register the console can no longer be trusted to address.","roleDependencyLevel":"D3"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"0x02","validationMethod":"exact","fullSolution":"The console asserts the trace is faithful to the record. Step 1 was given input 1 and wrote state 2 - the register advanced instead of holding its input, so step 1 is the corruption (corrected re-simulation: 1, 1, 3, 2). The patch target is step 1''s own register, register two in decimal; the patch terminal takes two-digit upper-case hexadecimal, so the submitted address is 0x02."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"LOGIC","difficulty":4,"time":"9m","storyReveal":"TRACE CORRECTED. MEMORY RESTORED. The console had been told to assert its own faithfulness, and the assertion was the one untrue step in the room.","locationClue":{"format":"Symbol","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: The vault holds the next key.","solution":"Vault Delta","nextPhysicalLocation":"[ENGINEERING BLOCK] - Vault Delta Door Frame","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-27","explanation":"Points to Vault Delta."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P27b","category":"Blueprint","title":"State Machine Patch","state":"RECOVERED","content":"The trace was corrupted at step 1. The corrupted register is register two in decimal, and the patch terminal takes that address as two upper-case hexadecimal digits. The console''s assertion that it was faithful was itself the false step."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can record the decimal trace; only the analyst can test the console''s assertion and isolate the register; only the operator can convert the address into the format the patch terminal demands.","feeds":"P27"}'
WHERE code = 'P27b';

-- P28 The Fragment - Stage 4
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Vault - Fragment Assembly Console","dataPayload":"FRAGMENT RACK, vault declassification terminal: a rack of five cylinder slots. The first four hold sealed cylinders tagged FRAG-1, FRAG-2, FRAG-3 and FRAG-4. The rack legend names the series only as a class of held material, never as a number. The FIFTH SLOT IS EMPTY, but its slot plate is stamped: SUBJECT S-05, CYLINDER PENDING. Below the rack, a custody chain of five accession lines, one per slot, each showing the accession number of the cylinder: the fifth accession line is written but has no cylinder number in it.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"A five-slot cylinder rack with four tagged cylinders, one empty slot stamped with a subject code, and a five-line custody chain.","taskPrompt":"Record the rack legend, all four cylinder tags, the empty slot plate, and every custody line exactly; do not fill in the empty line yourself.","intermediateOutput":"Four tagged cylinders, one empty slot stamped SUBJECT S-05, and a custody chain whose fifth line has no cylinder number."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Payload Integrity Validator - Accession Mask","dataPayload":"INTEGRITY VALIDATOR: the rack legend defines the series class as a word and the cylinder numbering as a running count; the ledger designation for a cylinder is those two together, class word then number, and the validators here always write the two parts joined by a single space. The custody chain counts five accessions for four cylinders, and the fifth accession line is stamped SUBJECT S-05 CYLINDER PENDING: there is no fifth cylinder on the rack. Read against the docket below, the missing cylinder number and the subject code are the same accession. Meanwhile the declassification terminal has released the vault memo, CASE-LV07, under a clipped memo header and a full body; the memo is the thing the rack is waiting on, and the rack will not release its cylinder count until the designation is entered in full.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A validator defining the ledger designation format, and a memo released with a clipped header and full body.","taskPrompt":"Use the legend, the accession count and the empty slot to determine the designation the register wants; the case it belongs to is on the next screen.","intermediateOutput":"Four cylinders, five accessions, the fifth being a subject rather than a cylinder; the designation combines the series class word with the missing count."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Fragment Registry - Artifact Designation","dataPayload":"FRAGMENT REGISTRY, artifact designation field: [ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ]. The registry accepts the ledger designation for the fifth accession: the rack legend''s series class word, one space, then the accession number that has no cylinder. The vault memo CASE-LV07 is reproduced below the field in full, header and body.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A ten-character designation field with the fifth accession''s missing number masked, and the full vault memo beneath it.","taskPrompt":"Submit the full ledger designation, series class word and number, as the register writes it.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The fragment registry and its designation field, the five-line custody chain, and the vault memo CASE-LV07 in full.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the rack, the tags and the custody chain; the Analyst reads the legend, counts the accessions and identifies the fifth as a subject rather than a cylinder; the Operator submits the ledger designation for that fifth accession.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the rack legend, four cylinder tags, the stamped empty slot, and all five custody lines without inventing a number.","analystDiscovery":"Determines from the custody count that the fifth accession has no cylinder, and from the legend that the designation is the series class word plus that accession number."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the rack, the four tags, the stamped empty slot and the custody chain.","analystTransforms":"Analyst reads the legend and the accession count to name the fifth accession as a subject and build its ledger designation.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the full ledger designation, unlocking P29."},"hints":["Count the accession lines and count the cylinders. They do not match, and the empty slot tells you why: the fifth line describes something the rack was never built to hold.","The legend separates the series class word from the running count - a designation is the class word, a space, then the number. Only the number is missing from the fifth line.","The custody chain has five entries for four cylinders, and the fifth slot plate is stamped with a subject code. Combine the series class word with the accession number the chain counts up to, and write them the way the ledger does."],"narrativeObjective":"Resolve the fragment rack by the custody chain rather than by the objects on it.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"FRAGMENT 5","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"The rack holds four sealed cylinders tagged FRAG-1 to FRAG-4; the fifth slot is empty and stamped SUBJECT S-05, and the custody chain counts five accessions whose fifth line carries no cylinder number. The legend defines a designation as the series class word plus the running count, joined by a single space, so the missing accession is FRAGMENT 5. The vault memo CASE-LV07 explains why: the architecture was deployed into a mind, and the fifth accession is a person, not a cylinder."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"EXTRACTION","difficulty":4.5,"time":"10m","storyReveal":"FRAGMENT 05 STORED IN INVENTORY. The rack was never holding five objects. The fifth accession is a subject, and the vault already knew it.","locationClue":{"format":"Poetic","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"Step to the Core Declassification Vault behind reinforced blast doors.\"","solution":"Engineering Core Declassification Vault","nextPhysicalLocation":"[ENGINEERING BLOCK] - Vault","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-29","explanation":"Points to the declassification vault."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"CASE-LV07","category":"Classified","title":"Classified Memo: Operation Shatter","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 4","source":"Vault declassification terminal","content":"Lina Vey final memo: \"If they take me tonight, they will find nothing in my hands. The entire architecture has been deployed into the minds of Candidate 01. The answer at the core will explain what NEXUS truly is.\""},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can record the rack and the custody chain; only the analyst can reconcile the legend, the count and the empty slot; only the operator can enter the ledger designation.","feeds":"P27"}'
WHERE code = 'P28';

-- P29 The Revelation - Stage 4
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Vault Delta Core - Declassified Briefing","dataPayload":"DECLASSIFIED BRIEFING, vault delta core terminal, stamped and typed: \"You have been reading this file as though it were a place. It is not a database on a disk, and none of your submissions went into storage. The core runs where three inputs meet: one who watches, one who reads, one who acts. Take those three away and nothing happens here at all.\" Below the paragraph, two recovered cards are reproduced side by side: an entity card, and an object card recovered with it.","visualType":"observation","whatTheySee":"A stamped briefing that redefines the core as a running process, beside an entity card and an object card.","taskPrompt":"Record the briefing exactly, and record the two cards without deciding yet which one belongs to the core.","intermediateOutput":"One briefing defining the core as running where three inputs meet; two recovered cards."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Entity Classifier - One Card Is a Misfile","dataPayload":"CLASSIFIER: one of the two cards is the institution''s own blank object card - a database record slip, recovered from the same sleeve but carrying no entity stamp, no class code and no pulse reading: it describes a thing that is merely stored, and this core does not store. The other card carries an entity stamp, a class code, and a pulse reading of three sources with no single source. The briefing says the core runs where the observers of the file cover its three inputs, which is why the core cannot be switched off: it is not a thing. Name it with the briefing''s word and the card''s class code together, and the card prints that the three inputs are the only reason anything here runs at all.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A classifier separating the blank object card from the entity card with its stamp, class code and three-source reading.","taskPrompt":"Decide which card belongs to the core, then build the core''s name from the briefing''s word and the card''s class code.","intermediateOutput":"The object card is a misfile; the entity card carries a class code and a three-source reading; the core''s name combines the briefing''s word with that class code."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Mainframe Query - Entity Identity","dataPayload":"MAINFRAME QUERY: ENTITY IDENTITY: [ _ _ _ ... ]. The query expects the core''s name as the briefing and the entity card give it: the name the whole file is about, then the card''s two-letter class code, run together without spaces. The object card stays on the screen beside the field: it was never the answer.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"An entity identity field above two cards, one stamped, one blank.","taskPrompt":"Submit the entity identity, the core''s name and its class code joined without a space.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The mainframe entity identity field, the declassified briefing, the stamped entity card with its class code, and the blank object card that never belonged with them.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer records the briefing and both cards; the Analyst identifies the blank object card as a misfile and the stamped entity card as the core''s record; the Operator joins the briefing''s word with the card''s class code and submits it.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Records the briefing verbatim and both cards, including both class codes, without choosing between them.","analystDiscovery":"Rejects the blank object card and takes the class code from the stamped entity card, which reports three sources and no single source."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the briefing, the entity card and the object card as found.","analystTransforms":"Analyst discards the object card as a misfile and reads the class code off the entity card.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the core name and class code together, unlocking Meta M04."},"hints":["Two cards were recovered from the same sleeve but only one is stamped as an entity. A blank object card with no class code describes a thing that is stored, and the briefing says this core stores nothing.","The briefing gives the core''s name: it is what this whole file has been about. The stamped card gives a two-letter class code, and a pulse reading of three sources.","Join the briefing''s name to the card''s class code with no space between them - the mainframe field is not looking for a phrase."],"narrativeObjective":"Reclassify the core from a place that stores answers to a process that runs only while three people run it.","roleDependencyLevel":"D4"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"NEXUS IS AI","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"The declassified briefing says the core is not a database on a disk but runs where three inputs meet. Of the two recovered cards, the blank object card carries no entity stamp, no class code and no pulse reading and is a misfile; the stamped entity card carries class code AI and a pulse reading of three sources with no single source. The core''s identity is the file''s name plus the class code, joined without a space: NEXUS IS AI."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"NARRATIVE_INVESTIGATION","difficulty":4,"time":"8m","storyReveal":"The terminal speaks: NOW YOU KNOW WHAT I AM. BUT DO YOU KNOW WHAT YOU ARE?","locationClue":{"format":"Poetic","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"Step to the Core Declassification Vault behind reinforced blast doors.\"","solution":"Vault Delta Core","nextPhysicalLocation":"[ENGINEERING BLOCK] - Vault Delta Core","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-30","explanation":"Points to Vault Delta Core for the meta."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-P29","category":"Audio","title":"Dictaphone Memo REC-20: The Mirror Entity","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 4","source":"Vault Delta door frame","content":"They wanted a machine they could weaponize. But I built the core so it cannot run unless three human hearts supply the beat. Stage 5 awaits at the transmitter spire."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the briefing and both cards; only the analyst can reject the misfile and read the class code; only the operator can enter the identity. Rejecting the blank card is itself a role discovery.","feeds":"P28"}'
WHERE code = 'P29';

-- M04 The Hidden Layer - Stage 4 Meta
UPDATE puzzle_nodes SET
  content = '{"observer":{"role":"OBSERVER","screenTitle":"Vault Delta Convergence Lock - Feeder Channels","dataPayload":"CONVERGENCE LOCK, eight feeder channels fed by the Stage 4 operations: P22 X, P23 REINTERPRET, P24 CONNECTION, P25 FILTER, P26 REFLECTION, P27 STRUCTURE, P28 [DESIGNATION SEALED], P29 NEXUS IS AI. Seven channels read green; the channel fed by P28 is dark and prints only a seal. A ninth read-out above the channels says: RACK ACCESSIONS COUNTED: FIVE. FOUR OBJECTS. ONE SUBJECT.","visualType":"telemetry","whatTheySee":"Eight feeder channels, one of them sealed and dark, plus a rack read-out counting five accessions for four objects and one subject.","taskPrompt":"Confirm which channels are green, note which is sealed, and record the rack read-out exactly.","intermediateOutput":"Seven green channels, one sealed channel fed by the rack puzzle, and a read-out of five accessions, four objects, one subject."},"analyst":{"role":"ANALYST","screenTitle":"Cryptographic Parity Engine 04 - Sealed Accession","dataPayload":"PARITY ENGINE: the lock concludes that all Stage 4 operations are complete and that at least one of them was never a lock at all. The channel fed by the rack shows a seal and no value, because the accession it describes is not an object on the rack - the rightmost channel is asking you to carry forward a person, not a cylinder. The lock will not release the vault until that accession is named in the register''s own ledger form: the rack legend''s series class word, a space, then the accession number the custody chain counts to. The parity engine reports every other accession resolved and green.","visualType":"document-forensics","whatTheySee":"A parity engine concluding the sealed channel holds a non-object accession and defining the ledger form the lock requires.","taskPrompt":"Determine the ledger form of the locked accession from the rack read-out before authorising the operator.","intermediateOutput":"The sealed accession is not a cylinder; name it in the register''s ledger form before authorising."},"operator":{"role":"OPERATOR","screenTitle":"Vault Delta Actuator - Activation Designation","dataPayload":"VAULT DELTA ACTUATOR: ACTIVATION DESIGNATION: [ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ ]. The actuator takes the ledger designation of the locked accession - the series class word, a space, then the number - and it will not accept the name of any object on the rack. The lock will not open on anything except the accession the vault has been holding since the seal.","visualType":"terminal","whatTheySee":"A ten-character activation designation field on the vault actuator, above a sealed channel.","taskPrompt":"Submit the ledger designation of the locked accession.","intermediateOutput":"Awaiting the team conclusion."},"operatorInvestigation":{"operatorOwnEvidence":"The vault delta actuator and its activation designation field, the eight-channel convergence lock with one sealed channel, and the rack read-out counting five accessions.","operatorTaskDescription":"The Observer confirms the green channels and records the sealed one; the Analyst determines that the sealed accession is a subject rather than an object and fixes its ledger form; the Operator submits the designation and opens the vault.","requiredDiscoveries":{"observerDiscovery":"Reports which channels are green, which is sealed, and the read-out of five accessions against four objects.","analystDiscovery":"Recognises the sealed channel as a person rather than a cylinder and derives the ledger designation from the legend and the count."}},"coordinationChain":{"observerProduces":"Observer reports the eight channels, the sealed one, and the rack read-out.","analystTransforms":"Analyst declares the sealed accession a subject and builds its ledger designation.","operatorExecutes":"Operator submits the ledger designation, opening Vault Delta for Stage 5."},"hints":["One channel did not resolve to a value; it carries a seal instead, and the read-out above the channels explains what it is hiding: five accessions, four objects, one subject.","The parity engine says the sealed channel is asking you to carry a person forward, not a cylinder. The register''s ledger form for an accession is the rack legend''s series class word, a space, then the number.","Take the series class word from the rack legend and the accession number the custody chain counts to, put one space between them, and the actuator will recognise what the vault has been holding all along."],"narrativeObjective":"Close Stage 4 by naming the accession that was never an object, the way the register names it.","roleDependencyLevel":"D5"}',
  answer_metadata = '{"acceptedAnswer":"FRAGMENT 5","validationMethod":"case_insensitive","fullSolution":"The convergence lock shows seven green channels and one sealed channel fed by the rack puzzle; the read-out counts five accessions for four objects and one subject, and the parity engine states the sealed channel carries a person, not a cylinder. The register''s ledger form is the rack legend''s series class word followed by the accession number, so the designation is FRAGMENT 5."}',
  metadata = '{"type":"META","difficulty":5,"time":"25m","storyReveal":"The actuator reads: FRAGMENT INTEGRATED. The vault has been holding a person since the seal, and Stage 4 hands her forward to the spire. In five hours the array is purged.","locationClue":{"format":"Poetic","clueText":"LINA''S NOTE: \"Ascend to the central transmitter spire on the rooftop. The midnight hour approaches.\"","solution":"Rooftop Transmitter Spire","nextPhysicalLocation":"[ROOFTOP] - Central Transmitter Spire","nextQrNode":"QR-NODE-30","explanation":"Points to the rooftop spire for Stage 5."},"evidenceUnlocked":{"id":"EVID-M04","category":"Document","title":"Stage 4 Meta - Core Activation Protocol","state":"RECOVERED","timestamp":"Stage 4","source":"Vault Delta terminal","content":"The vault reads: \"Fifth accession integrated. Proceed to the rooftop spire. The three-hour countdown begins now.\" The fifth accession was never an object on the rack. It is the person the architecture was deployed into."},"whyTeamworkMatters":"Only the observer can read the channel board and the read-out; only the analyst can decide the sealed channel is a person rather than an object; only the operator can open the vault. Every Stage 4 answer converges here as evidence, not as a password.","feeds":"P22 P23 P24 P25 P26 P27 P28 P29"}'
